## Tools essential for building
- Install all of them in one command

    sudo apt-get install git build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev libtool-bin libtool automake autoconf libxslt1-dev libxml2-dev libcurl4-gnutls-dev bc fakeroot zip libpcap-dev

- Install all of them in one command, if for Debian 7 Wheezy

    sudo apt-get install git build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev libtool automake autoconf libxslt1-dev libxml2-dev libcurl4-gnutls-dev bc fakeroot zip libpcap-dev
    - libtool-bin is not a separate package in Wheezy

## Components for building
- libc6-i386
  - Used for building ppc
    Description: GNU C Library: 32-bit shared libraries for AMD64
    This package includes shared versions of the standard C
    ibrary and the standard math library, as well as many others.
    This is the 32bit version of the library, meant for AMD64 systems.

- bc --needed by KERNEL build
- libcurl4-gnutls-dev
- zip, needed for building `gcc`
- build-essential, to compile C and C++
- autoconf (aclocal, autoconf)
- automake
- libtool
- libtool-bin (for netconf now, TODO: use maintained one if not available on build host.)
- libssl
    - TODO: Provide a choice to use build host libssl, or use a maintained fixed version.
    - TODO: By default, check build host libssl, if not available, use the maintained one.
    - TODO: Or, provide them in SDK / Tool chain
- pkg-config
  - Use this for lib/include detecting, please.
- libpcap-dev
    - To provide /usr/include/pcap.h /usr/include/pcap/pcap.h
    - Needed now by sflow/sflowsocket.hh

## Toolchain
- Although eldk-5.3 contains PowerPC toolchain, we stayed at eldk4.2 to build all the BCM SDK on PPC platfom.
- Only ARM toolchain from eldk-5.3 is used, only for as4610.
    - eldk-5.3/armv7a/sysroots/armv7a-vfp-neon-linux-gnueabi, which is based on BCM arm cpu.
- We had no MARVELL product active now.
    - gnueabi/arm-none-linux-gnueabi_SDK-1.2.4-alpha/ might be used for MARVELL platform, which is no longer updated for several years.

- /opt/eldk4.2
    - For building SDK for arm, powerpc
- /opt/eldk-5.3
    - For building others for arm, powerpc
- /opt/bitbake
    - For `yocto` building
- gnueabi/arm-none-linux-gnueabi_SDK-1.2.4-alpha
    - Obsolete
- x86 tool chain
    - TODO

> $PATH, had been added with profile

