# Build tasks

- [x] Env dependency
  - [x] NO interfere with build server env
      - Only export env during building process, to avoid break system env
      - Done. By binding ENV with each BOX, in kernel/sdk/pica/xorp/ovs

- [ ] Speed improvements
  - [ ] Top level initiating using `make`
      - [ ] Best for increamental buidling
  - [ ] Separate build tree
      - [ ] Use BUILD_DIR or such alike
      - Now hard-coded by `top_srcdir`; Need to replace it
  - [ ] SDK
      - [x] ALMOST Done, by Richard, not well tested
      - [ ] `.ko` abstraction
    - [ ] Separate build tree for SDK
      - [ ] Each tree for one combination of `ARCH+CHIPSET`

- Other improvements, for easy maintenance, etc.
  - [x] Unify ovs/pica/xorp build script
      - [x] Unified naming
        - [x] One sh file, with BOX name as parameters to call
      - [ ] TODO: To init build from any location, using pushd/popd
        - [x] Or using `OLDPWD=$PWD`
  - [x] Remove PICA8=1 for builds except SDK
  - [x] DONE. ~~BRANCH using name of current branch~~
  - [x] Unify make all/fast
      - DONE.
  - [x] BOX=1, such as AS5712_54X=1, can be removed.
      - `Makefile` had defined them all.
  - [ ] SDK to be determined by BOX name
      - BCM, 6.3.9, 6.4.7, 6.5.4, 6.5.11, etc.
      - CVM
      - MVL
      - MTK
      - Different version of one vender in respective branches
        - Richard had split that, and managed using `repo` manifest.xml
  - [x] Keep build dir for easy trouble shooting
    - Cleaning should be with `make clean`, rather than `git clean`
    - Keep build_image dev.tar.gz rootfs-debian
        - [ ] build_deb ram_disk ramdisk_deb
        - [ ] Partly done.

  - [x] No `sudo`, anymore
      - Done, use `fakeroot`
        - To avoid using `sudo`, added before `make` when using `mknod` or explode tarballs with nodes, etc.
        - Using "sudo" during build to get superuser privilege to make dev nodes, etc. was very dangerous. (imagine an bug like "rm -fr /  * " run by sudo...)
        - That would generate tmp dirs/files owned by root hard to clean using normal "make clean" or "git clean" or "git checkout" or "git reset".
        - Common practice is to use fakeroot, a tool for simulating superuser privileges.
        - Or you can try other jail/chroot/fake/container env tools.
        - From 2.7.1, using `fakeroot`, replacing `sudo`

  - [ ] Enable DEBUG global switch option
      - For `debug` build only, not in `release` build
      - [ ] DEBUG builds will carry symbol tables, perf tools, etc.
        - tecla
          - http://www.astro.caltech.edu/~mcs/tecla/
          - Currently not submodule; it's now copied as folders, hard to sync with upstream patches
        - tcl
          - For internal regression/automation
  - [ ] `debug` build next step modules
        - netconf
          - Currently not submodule; it's now copied as folders, hard to sync with upstream patches
        - libnetconf
          - Currently not submodule; it's now copied as folders, hard to sync with upstream patches
        - net-snmp
          - Currently not submodule; it's now copied as folders, hard to sync with upstream patches
        - pyang
        - [iperf](iperf) for traffic performance benchmarking
        - gperftool, profiling/benchmarking tools
        - https://github.com/ocpnetworking-wip/oom
          - A project for Optical module monitoring

- http://vmiklos.hu/blog/sparse-checkout-example-in-git-1-7
        - Other debug/trace/log tools
      - [ ] DEBUG builds will automatically transfer core dumps to `dump server`
        - To avoid losing them in case of re-flashing boxes
      - [ ] For docker/VM/QEMU, enable DEBUG mode for internal usage
        - Add ssh key pairs for easy debug
        - debug options during build
      - DO NOT include DEBUG mode into release builds
        - Less build trime
        - Remove unnecessary contents in final image

