    --with-license

# customization variants building
Refer to [box-info](box-info.md)

## Purpose

- A single base that covers common features
- In response to requests by different needs to implement various requirements

## Guidelines
- All commits go to baseline branch
  - easy to sync, esp for major fixes
  - less regression issue
- Enable/Disable features through variant customization, i.e. OEM build
  - collected variant requirement
  - easy to build, test track

## customization contents for requirements
  - Base build by default shows the Pica8 DEFINDED values, logo and description, etc.
    - Or to provide placeholders to be finalized at OEM build using our own default suite
  - Working mode: OVS/XorPlus/CLi, etc.
  - Interface
    - IP configuration on management interface: DHCP/Static
    - Ability to easily switch to alternate service or components
      - Thus allows more partner and solutions to promote, upsale/prosale us
    - etc.
  - Branding / Wording / LOGO, etc.
    - Welcome message
    - Changing the login appearance, company identity, branded slogin
    - etc.
  - Misc customization configurations
    - passwd modification
    - URLs
    - etc.

## Example
- `verizon_itnuc` image is generated based on normal common/base image, with OEM configurations, using `build-oem`.


## Design
- Base build + OEM customization build
- Plugin style interface with flexibly of addition of other features in future

## Where to define?

```
/* Brand name */
#define BRAND_NAME "Pica8"     >  Luxar Tech
/* Host name */
#define HOST_NAME "XorPlus"    >  XorPlus
/* Platform name */
#define PLATFORM_NAME "PicOS"   >   LNOS
/* company name */
#define COMPANY_NAME "Pica8, Inc"   >  Luxar Tech, Inc.

```

