### TODO: Unify show_version.sh into only one version.sh
Changes:
    No /pica/bin/show_version.sh, only one /pica/bin/version.sh
        They are almost the same.

    /pica/bin/version.sh would be copied also as /usr/bin/version.
        To keep as less change in CLI, this copy is kept.

All calls to /pica/bin/show_version.sh or /pica/bin/version.sh will now call version, which is in /usr/bin/version

Result:

        admin@XorPlus$/pica/bin/version.sh
        Copyright (C) 2009-2016 Vcmy, Inc..
        ===================================
        Hardware Model                : VCMY-S6000-48X
        Base ethernet MAC Address     : 70:72:cf:90:9a:31
        Linux System Version/Revision : 2.6.5S1/c218006
        Linux System Released Date    : 05/04/2016
        L2/L3 Version/Revision        : 2.6.5S1/c218006
        L2/L3 Released Date           : 05/04/2016
        OVS/OF Version/Revision       : 2.6.5S1/c218006
        OVS/OF Released Date          : 05/04/2016


NOTE:

        There is plan to change date format from
        05/04/2016
        to 2016-04-05

        And change Version/Revision from "2.6.5S1/c218006" to "2.6.5S1+c218006"

    If so, we should change "-F/" to "-F+"

    Or, just leave the date format as so.


