cc1: all warnings being treated as errors
```

- Cause
Code has warnings.

- Solution
Change code to remove all warnings. [Recommended]

- Solution
ignore warnings being treated as errors

If you know exact warnings to be ignored.

    CFLAGS="-Wno-error=unused-but-set-variable -Wno-error=unused-but-set-parameter"

Or You can also replace your -Werror compiler options with -Werror -Wno-error=cpp
```
-Wno-error=cpp
-Wno-error=#warnings
```

Or globally in Makefile

    -Werror

Or globally in configure

    --disable-werror

### virtual memory exhausted: Cannot allocate memory
```
virtual memory exhausted: Cannot allocate memory
make[4]: *** [area_router.lo] Error
```

Or
```
virtual memory exhaustedvirtual memory exhausted: virtual memory exhaustedCannot allocate memoryvirtual memory exhausted
: : Cannot allocate memory
Cannot allocate memory
virtual memory exhausted: Cannot allocate memory
```

- Cause
virtual memory exhausted

- Solution
Enable swap, or restrict the amount of virtual memory allowed

To avoid this, create a small swap partition, or swap file.

```
           Device Boot      Start         End      Blocks   Id  System
        /dev/sdd1   *        2048  1919080447   959539200   83  Linux
        /dev/sdd2      1919082494  1952446463    16681985    5  Extended
        /dev/sdd5      1919082496  1952446463    16681984   82  Linux swap / Solaris
```

Before:
```
        $ free
                     total       used       free     shared    buffers     cached
        Mem:       8147408    7373556     773852          0    1809988    1340136
        -/+ buffers/cache:    4223432    3923976
        Swap:            0          0          0
```

Enable swap.

        $ sudo swapon  /dev/sdd5

After:
```
        $ free
                     total       used       free     shared    buffers     cached
        Mem:       8147408    7789688     357720          0    1600700    2554016
        -/+ buffers/cache:    3634972    4512436
        Swap:     16681980          0   16681980
```

Although the performance won't improve too much, the error can be avoided.
Thus the build can continue without breaking due to this "memory exhausted".

- Solution
restrict the amount of virtual memory allowed

Use the ulimit command to restrict the amount of virtual memory allowed.

```
$ ulimit -a

core file size          (blocks, -c) 0
data seg size           (kbytes, -d) unlimited
scheduling priority             (-e) 0
file size               (blocks, -f) unlimited
pending signals                 (-i) 31545
max locked memory       (kbytes, -l) 64
max memory size         (kbytes, -m) unlimited
open files                      (-n) 65536
pipe size            (512 bytes, -p) 8
POSIX message queues     (bytes, -q) 819200
real-time priority              (-r) 0
stack size              (kbytes, -s) 8192
cpu time               (seconds, -t) unlimited
max user processes              (-u) 31545
virtual memory          (kbytes, -v) unlimited
file locks                      (-x) unlimited

$ ulimit -m 60000

$ ulimit -m
60000
```

### source file '../dummy_main.cc' is in a subdirectory,
```
...
bgp/harness/Makefile.am:85: warning: 'INCLUDES' is the old name for 'AM_CPPFLAGS' (or '*_CPPFLAGS')
bgp/harness/Makefile.am:47: warning: source file '../dummy_main.cc' is in a subdirectory,
bgp/harness/Makefile.am:47: but option 'subdir-objects' is disabled
automake: warning: possible forward-incompatibility.
automake: At least a source file is in a subdirectory, but the 'subdir-objects'
```

### \' is already registered with AC_CONFIG_FILES.

CRLF problem.

Make sure that configure.ac is LF-only.

> autoconf/status.m4:848: AC_CONFIG_FILES is expanded from...
> configure.ac:3814: the top level
> Autom4te::FileUtils::xsystem(/usr/autotool/devel/share/autocon
> f/Autom4te/FileUtils.pm:29
>
> Please note the single single-quote at the beginning of the
> error message. I have included the command line after the
> main body of this post.

Bad EOL type problem.  That's not a single quote: it's a singly-quoted
  string which ends with an LF (but no CR) causing the closing quote and
  remainder of the error message to be output on the same line overwriting
  whatever it actaully was that was 'already registered with....'


## Autotools related
### linking libtool libraries using a non-POSIX
```
ltlibrary.am: warning: 'libxx.la': linking libtool libraries using a non-POSIX
```

### ltlibrary.am: archiver requires 'AM_PROG_AR' in 'configure.ac'

AM_PROG_AR was introduced in automake 1.11.2.  As per the docs for
AM_PROG_AR, it is supposed to be included when the archiver ('ar') is
used, but prior to automake 1.12 the warning was only shown iff
-Wextra-portability was specified.  automake 1.12 introduced a change
that includes -Wextra-portability when -Wall is specified.

```diff
 configure.ac | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac


 AM_INIT_AUTOMAKE([1.11 foreign -Wall no-define no-dist-gzip dist-xz])
 AM_SILENT_RULES([yes])
+m4_ifdef([AM_PROG_AR], [AM_PROG_AR]) dnl Workaround for Automake 1.12

 # Initialize libtool
 LT_PREREQ([2.2])
```

